# Drafted by Gemini (R26 keeps), edited. What the Moon Keeps: four keepsakes, one for each Act.

~ start
the_vagrant [sly]: The moon keeps what the dead lose, you know, and four small things of yours are tucked right inside its pockets, one from each leg of your journey.
set mf_keeps_asked
quest mf_what_moon_keeps asked
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask where they might be -> where
* [if item:mf_keepsake_1 or item:mf_keepsake_2 or item:mf_keepsake_3 or item:mf_keepsake_4] Show him what we have found -> hand_over
* [ends:mf_what_moon_keeps] Tell him to leave them to the moon -> left
* Take our leave -> END

~ where
the_vagrant [neutral]: The first fell right here on my platform, the second out in the farmland, the third down in the Maidenmist dark, and the fourth upon that burning hill.
-> menu

~ hand_over
if item:mf_keepsake_1
take mf_keepsake_1
set mf_keepsakes += 1
endif
if item:mf_keepsake_2
take mf_keepsake_2
set mf_keepsakes += 1
endif
if item:mf_keepsake_3
take mf_keepsake_3
set mf_keepsakes += 1
endif
if item:mf_keepsake_4
take mf_keepsake_4
set mf_keepsakes += 1
endif
if flag.mf_keepsakes >= 4
-> all_found
else
-> some_found
endif

~ some_found
the_vagrant [neutral]: That is some of it, at least, though I reckon the rest of your missing pieces are still waiting out there in the dark somewhere.
-> menu

~ all_found
the_vagrant [smile]: There now, that is everything laid out neat and proper, so tell me what you would like an old conductor to do with them.
* Let him carry them on the train -> returned
* Keep them close ourselves -> kept

~ returned
the_vagrant [smile]: I will lock them up tight in the baggage car for you, and you can claim them with your ticket once all this business is over.
quest mf_what_moon_keeps returned
bless party 2h
-> END

~ kept
the_vagrant [smile]: That is fair enough, I suppose, since small things always want to be near their people, and I have plenty of empty cloth to fold away.
quest mf_what_moon_keeps kept
inspiration party
-> END

~ left
the_vagrant [weary]: The moon can keep them for good, then, and truth be told, she will probably look after them better than most folk down here ever could.
quest mf_what_moon_keeps left
-> END
